		<unit label="chapter" identifier="22" level="3">Planning, Subdivision of Land and Zoning</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="2" level="4">Local Planning Commissions</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>15.2-2215</section_number>
	<catch_line>Quorum majority vote</catch_line>
	<text>
		A majority of the members shall constitute a quorum and no action of the local planning commission shall be valid unless authorized by a majority vote of those present and voting.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 15-963.3; 1962, c. 407, § 15.1-440; 1974, c. 99; 1975, c. 641; 1997, c. 587.</history>
</law>
